# C5 — first numerical divergence, local review result

## Direct result

**`NATIVE_SHAPE_EFFECT_CAUSALLY_LOCALIZED` at layer 0, absolute token 0, native CPU `ggml_flash_attn_ext`.** The 113-ID case is stable within each form: A1=A2 for ub32 and B1=B2 for ub64, all 201088 final F32 logits bitwise. A/B differ in 201087 logits, as C4 reported. All C5 observers were final-logit neutral within each form after one preserved empty-last-layer observer failure. The first equal captured tensor is `attn_norm-0`; Q/K/V projections, biases, reshapes and Q/K RoPE remain bitwise equal across all 113 positions. The first observed different output is `__fattn__-0` in the first chunk, at token0/feature0, **before MoE**.

The native operator alone reproduces both observed outputs bitwise with each form's captured Q/K/V, causal mask and sinks. On one common B input, grouping 32 queries gives the A32 bytes; grouping 64 changes 130907 of 131072 F32 elements in the first32 outputs (max absolute 0.01181817, RMSE 0.000428419). Forcing the pinned GGML CPU `use_ref` vector path **at the same B64 shape** restores the A32 bytes in those rows. Source fixes the Flash Attention Q tile at 64, uses a vector branch for 32 queries and a tiled branch for 64 with these captured types. The vector branch converts Q to F16 for its dot product and accumulates F16 V; the tiled branch packs Q/K to F32 and uses F32 GEMM/V accumulation. This controlled native intervention identifies the path change causing the first output difference. It does not establish which form has better generation quality.

| Gate | C5 result / scope |
|---|---|
| Stability | `A/A BITWISE_PASS`, `B/B BITWISE_PASS`, `A/B DIVERGENCE_REPRODUCED` on fresh-process exact 113-ID b256 controls |
| Capture | `NEUTRAL_BITWISE` within ub32 and ub64 for repaired layer, operation, QKV, attention and source observers; callback timings have no performance authority |
| First operation | `ggml_flash_attn_ext`, layer0 CPU/SWA, token0/feature0; 261964/462848 logical Flash output F32 values differ over 113 positions, max abs0.01295853 |
| Input/state | First32 Q rows, visible K/V cells, causal mask and sinks are bytewise equal; query0 sees only key0; no inferred equivalence from cache counters |
| Native replay | A32 and B64 same-form outputs match full-model captures bitwise; B32 common-input and B64 `use_ref` first32 outputs match A32 bitwise |
| Cause / defect | `NATIVE_SHAPE_EFFECT_CAUSALLY_LOCALIZED`; no C5 streaming/backend bug demonstrated, no correction patch |
| Candidate | ub64 still `NON_BITWISE_REQUIRES_SEPARATE_QUALIFICATION`, not promoted; no performance, sampling or default claim |
| W waves | `NOT_RUN`; first-divergence mission complete without a wave-capacity patch |

## Authority and limits

The prospective gate is [C5 protocol](C5-PROTOCOL-20260927.md), chronological evidence is in [C5 ledger](C5-LEDGER-20260927.md), and compact machine-readable comparisons are indexed by [results/INDEX.md](../results/INDEX.md). `results/c5-d1-comparison01.json` seals stable final logits. `results/c5-d2-layer-comparison01.json`, `c5-d2-op-comparison01.json`, `c5-d2-qkv-comparison01.json` and `c5-d2-attn-comparison01.json` narrow the first observed output. **`results/c5-d3-native-replay-summary01.json` is the causal operator authority**, including source tensor layouts, post-run hashes, exact bridges, common-input intervention and quantitative deltas. Exact commands, libraries, telemetry and binary identities are in the local run manifests; large raw tensors and binary outputs stay local/untracked.

The physical target was reconfirmed: Fedora ProArt PX13, Ryzen AI 9 HX 370, RTX 4060 Laptop 8188 MiB, internal NVMe GGUF SHA-256 `582bd40f6886200101f4c4ed9f25f3fe80cc14c86e9e2b37746cd8904a0c622d`; exact 113-ID file SHA-256 `368c48ac1e93d68ec1746bb3d5f7e63118f35d7903c58f88dbe5c983b69190fb`. Streaming backend remained `1248fd8fa8cfebaece5ea992e4d951c1e18bb9d5`, no backend/model change. Target runs used memory.max18 GiB, swap.max0, RSS17 GiB, GPU7000 MiB, MemAvailable6 GiB, 95/80/70 °C guards, preload OFF, direct I/O, GPU8 actual CPU0–28/GPU29–35, 32 slots, ctx4096, threads8/I/O4, external b256 and one requested final logit row. Highest C5 target cgroup peak among these controls was 15,379,492,864 B; GPU ≤3893 MiB, CPU ≤87.25 °C and NVMe ≤53.85 °C; no cgroup swap/max/OOM or monitor stop. Host zram used by other processes was not changed. The first observer failure was a C5 capture shape guard, not a resource or target-computation failure; its root is preserved.

The native replay is local operator evidence with the same captured Flash inputs and pinned mature GGML, not an independent full 120B reference. C4's 252/252 same-form resident MoE boundary rows remain valid for their captured ub64 states; this C5 origin precedes FFN, so a new same-input FFN differential was unnecessary to locate it. Exact full-model propagation from token0 to the final 201088-logit delta was not decomposed operator by operator; it was observed through the same neutral graph captures. The old C2/C3 free-generation discrepancy lacks original exact IDs/state and remains `HISTORICAL_ORIGIN_UNRESOLVED`. No sampler or distribution-preserving claim follows. A numerically new ub64 default would need a separate prospective qualification contract; the conservative ub32 no-preload profile is untouched. No C5 push, merge, PR, or publication is authorized. `BROAD_NOVELTY_NO_GO / ENGINEERING_AND_MEASUREMENT_GO`.

## Commands tested and preserved failures

Model-free: `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 -m unittest tools.test_c5_compare tools.test_c2_gate tools.test_c3_approval tools.test_c3_terminal_sample` passed **41/41**; compiled `tools/test_c4_prefill_clock` passed. D1 and each D2/D3 source run used `systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=19327352832 -p MemorySwapMax=0 -- python3 tools/run_bounded.py ... -- tools/c5_*_probe MODEL IDS PREFIX short --ubatch 32|64`; each manifest stores its unabridged effective command and environment. Native replay commands, executed without a model process: `tools/c5_flash_replay A32 normal results/c5-d3-replay-a32-normal01.f32`, `B64 normal`, `B32 normal`, `B64 ref`, `A32 ref` with their matching no-replace filenames; then `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 tools/c5_compare_flash_replay.py`. All native outputs were finite. The first D2 `c5-d2-capture-a-ub32-01` observer failed on the legitimate zero-row last layer, was not used, and led to a fresh repaired observer ID; no FAIL was overwritten. Closure verified no C5 process, NVIDIA compute app or llama listener remained; the GPU was idle at 23 MiB/44 °C. Local commits used unsigned mode because the signing agent refused operation.

Next allowed decision: either retain ub32 as default or design a **new, prospective numerical and sampling qualification** for the native shape change. No performance screening or default switch is justified by C5.
